  "answer": "This has been reported before. \"Open url in Edge\" is a fallback item, which is generated from the text you typed. Past tickets show that fallbacks can't be pinned to the Dock yet. The Dock records the pin but never shows it, which is what you're seeing. The maintainers said fallbacks probably shouldn't be pinnable at all, because they depend on the exact text passed to them. The planned fixes are to disable \"Pin to Dock\" on fallback items and to add a newer style of fallback that can be pinned. As a workaround, add your msteams:// link as a Bookmark in Command Palette, or use a shortcut, and pin that instead. Pinning bookmarks and shortcuts is reported to work. If a pin of a normal, non-fallback item doesn't show up, try quitting and relaunching Command Palette (PowerToys#47155, PowerToys#49025). That is a separate issue from this one."
